# Description: READ BINARY from offset 0 of the currently selected file.
# Category: reading
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
# Reads the beginning of whichever elementary file is currently selected.
# Select a file first, for example with the select_mf or select_ef_dir
# script; on its own, this command may fail with SW 69 86 ("no current EF")
# if no elementary file is selected. Reading does not modify the card.
#
# THE COMMAND, BYTE BY BYTE
#   00     class byte: standard interindustry commands
#   B0     instruction: READ BINARY
#   00 00  P1-P2 together form the 15-bit offset inside the file; here the
#          offset is 0, the very first byte of the file
#   00     Le: request 256 bytes (short Le 00 means 256)
#
# WHAT YOU SHOULD SEE
#   The file contents followed by SW 90 00. SW 6B 00 means the offset lies
#   outside the file; SW 69 86 means no elementary file is selected.
#
# This command does not write anything to the card.
00 B0 00 00 00
